---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from "../config/site";

const canonicalUrl = `${SITE_URL}/privacy-policy/`;

/**
 * Bump this whenever the substance of the policy changes — particularly if an
 * email signup, affiliate links, or any further third-party script is added.
 *
 * What this page must keep describing accurately, as of this date: Google
 * Analytics 4, the contact form, Cloudflare Turnstile, Cloudflare Email Sending,
 * Cloudflare Pages hosting, and Google Fonts.
 */
const lastUpdated = "August 16, 2026";
---

<Layout
	title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE_NAME}`}
	description={`How ${SITE_NAME}'s website handles visitor data.`}
	canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
	robots="index,follow"
>
	<div class="page page-narrow">
		<span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
		<hr class="rule-short" />
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--bone-3); margin-top: var(--space-4);">
			Last updated {lastUpdated}
		</p>

		<div class="prose" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
			<p class="lede">
				This is a static website. It has no accounts, no comment system, no advertising,
				and no mailing list. It has one contact form, and it uses Google Analytics only
				if you agree to it. Both are described below.
			</p>

			<h2>What this site collects</h2>

			<p>
				Only what you type into the contact form, and only when you choose to send it.
				There is no account system, nothing that records what you read, and no data
				gathered for advertising or sale.
			</p>

			<h2>Analytics</h2>

			<p>
				This site can use Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are
				read — but only if you agree. On your first visit a banner asks. Until you
				accept, the Google tag is never loaded: no analytics cookies are set, and no
				request is made to Google at all, so nothing about your visit reaches them.
				Declining is a single click, and the site works exactly the same either way.
			</p>

			<p>
				If you do accept, the tag sets cookies and reports information about your visit
				— pages viewed, approximate location derived from your IP address, browser,
				device type, and referring site — to Google, which processes it under its own
				privacy terms. It is used to understand what people read, not to identify
				individuals, and the data is not sold or combined with anything else collected
				here.
			</p>

			<p>
				Your answer is remembered in your browser's local storage, not in a cookie. You
				can change it at any time with the <button
					type="button"
					class="inline-link-button"
					data-cookie-preferences>Cookie choices</button
				> link in the footer of any page; withdrawing consent deletes the analytics cookies
				and reloads the page. Browser "do not track" settings, ad and tracker blockers, and
				Google's <a
					href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out add-on</a
				> all work as well.
			</p>

			<h2>The contact form</h2>

			<p>
				The contact form on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> asks for your name,
				email address, and message. When you send it, those are delivered by email to the
				site's own inbox and are kept only for as long as needed to correspond with you.
				They are not added to a mailing list, sold, or shared, and they aren't stored in
				a database — there isn't one.
			</p>

			<p>
				The form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, which checks that a submission
				comes from a person rather than a bot. Turnstile receives your IP address and
				some technical signals about your browser to make that assessment. Cloudflare
				states that it does not use this for cross-site tracking or advertising. Mail is
				then sent through Cloudflare's email service.
			</p>

			<h2>What the host records</h2>

			<p>
				The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes
				standard request data — IP address, browser user-agent, requested page, and
				timestamp — in order to deliver pages and protect the service from abuse. This is
				handled under Cloudflare's own privacy terms, and it is not used here to build a
				profile of you.
			</p>

			<h2>Fonts</h2>

			<p>
				Typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts. Your browser therefore makes a request to
				Google's servers, which discloses your IP address and user-agent to Google. No
				identifying information is sent by this site along with that request.
			</p>

			<h2>Links to other sites</h2>

			<p>
				Links to booksellers such as Amazon, and to social profiles such as X and
				Facebook, take you to services with their own privacy practices, which govern
				once you leave this site. These are plain links: no affiliate tracking, referral
				codes, or commissions are attached to them, and no widgets, embeds, or tracking
				scripts from those retailers or social networks run on this site.
			</p>

			<h2>Where this data goes</h2>

			<p>
				Nothing collected here is sold, rented, or shared for advertising. The only
				third parties involved are the ones named above — Google, for analytics and
				fonts, and Cloudflare, for hosting, spam checking, and delivering form mail —
				each acting under its own privacy terms. Analytics data is retained by Google
				according to the property's settings; contact-form mail is kept in an ordinary
				email inbox for as long as the correspondence is useful, then deleted.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>

			<p>
				This site is intended for adults and is not directed to children under 13.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>

			<p>
				If this policy changes — for instance, if a newsletter is ever added — the revised
				version will be posted here with a new date above.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>

			<p>
				Questions about this policy can go through the
				<a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
